.TH "strata-by-luminaire" "6" "2026-11-19" "Strata User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
strata-by-luminaire - the command to run Strata.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
strata-by-luminaire [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Strata is a 4k intro released by Luminaire in august 2015.
Ended 5th in the combined 4k competition at Assembly 2015.
.PP
The intro runs in a 1280x720 window, synchronized with the vertical
refresh.
The music is generated as raw audio (16 bits, stereo, 44100 Hz) on the
standard output of the intro, and the command pipes it to
\f[B]pw-play\f[R](1) when PipeWire runs, else to \f[B]paplay\f[R](1)
when PulseAudio runs, else to \f[B]aplay\f[R](1).
.PP
cyndis [code, graphics] Jontte [code, graphics] jnalanko [music]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
--help
Display help for the command
.PP
The intro stops by itself after 118 seconds.
Escape quits.
.SH NOTES
.PP
Only a packed 32-bit binary was released.
The Debian version is the unpacked binary, patched to stay in a window.
.PP
The binary is also patched at build time so that the picture is
displayed with current OpenGL drivers: with NVIDIA, the shader program
was never used and the window stayed white, and Mesa refused the shader.
The intro now quits cleanly at the end instead of crashing.
.SH INFOS
.PP
https://www.pouet.net/prod.php?which=66090
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]pw-play\f[R](1), \f[B]paplay\f[R](1), \f[B]aplay\f[R](1)
.SH BUGS
.PP
No known bugs.
